    "Fixed 256-bit membership set used by byte-wide find-first-of scans.",
    section("Representation and operations", "Four u64 words cover all u8 values. Construction clears the words; `add(byte)` sets its membership bit and `has(byte)` reads that bit, each in O(1). A scan builds the set in O(k) and tests n input bytes in O(n), without heap storage. The helper is an implementation kernel rather than a resizing public set container."),
